BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tween Crafternoon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T151500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T163000
UID:68a37e20709d27410037bafa@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Tweens ages 10-14 are welcome to join us and create a new art
  or craft project the 1st Thursday of each month!\nMarch 5: Perler Party
 \nApril 2:  Yarn Landscapes\nMay 7:  Design your own Zine
LOCATION:Banks Public Library\, Jane Moore Community Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/68a37e20709d27410037bafa
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Manga and Comics Workshop | Taller de Manga y Cómics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T190000
UID:69e2ef36c1cf6f9a7586242c@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to draw and paint manga and comic style art in our b
 eginner workshop! We'll teach you how to use both paper and fabrics as med
 iums so you can create your own incredible artwork not just in your notebo
 ok\, but on clothes\, backpacks\, totes\, and much more. Whether you're h
 oping to start writing that story stuck in your mind\, or just looking to
  add some flair to your style\, this workshop is the perfect place to see 
 your vision turn to reality!\nThis program is for teens ages 13-18.\n¡Apr
 ende a dibujar y pintar manga y cómics en nuestro taller para principiant
 es! Te enseñaremos a usar papel y tela para que puedas crear tus propias 
 obras de arte increíbles\, no solo en tu cuaderno\, sino también en ropa
 \, mochilas\, bolsos y mucho más. Ya sea que quieras empezar a escribir e
 sa historia que tienes en mente o simplemente darle un toque especial a tu
  estilo\, ¡este taller es el lugar perfecto para convertir tu visión en 
 realidad!\nEste programa está dirigido a adolescentes de 13 a 18 años.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e2ef36c1cf6f9a7586242c
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Read to the Dogs/Lee a los perros
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T170000
UID:6932400076261f28005d8d9a@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to build your skills and confidence? Read aloud to a trai
 ned therapy dog (accompanied by their handler) in a private 20-minute sess
 ion. Grades K – 12.\n¿Quieres mejorar tus habilidades y tu confianza? I
 nscríbete para leer en voz alta a perros de terapia (acompañados por un 
 entrenador) en una sesión privada de 20 minutos. K – 12o grado.\nYou ma
 y sign up for one(1) Read to the Dogs session within a one(1) month period
 .
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6932400076261f28005d8d9a
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Makerspace Open Lab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T173000
UID:69eea87afca21471b7f06737@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Makerspace Open Labs are for anyone who wants to check out the
  space and use our equipment to make cool things. Room assistants are avai
 lable to guide you in the basic use of the tools and technology. Come in w
 ith an idea and leave with a finished project! For more information about 
 the Makerspace and its resources\,\nsee here\n.\nMakerspace Open Labs take
  place on the following weekly schedule:\nTuesdays\n\, 5:30 - 7:30PM\nThur
 sdays\n\, 4:00 - 6:00PM\nSaturdays\n\, 10:00 AM - 1:00PM\nSundays\n\, 1:30
  - 5:30P\nEach month we provide the materials\, tools and instructions for
  a featured Makerspace project that everyone is invited to try.\nJune\n's 
 featured project is Clay Pot Mushrooms.\nIMPORTANT:\nAdults using the Make
 rspace for the first time need to\nsign a waiver\n\; people under the age 
 of 18 must have a waiver signed by a parent or guardian.\nYou can sign and
  submit waivers online here.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Makerspace
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69eea87afca21471b7f06737
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:One Book\, One Coast
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T160000
UID:698655718b29ea2800ce6916@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a library program uniting a network of West Coast 
 Libraries in a shared celebration of literacy\, learning\, community and c
 ivil discourse.\nThe One Book\, One Coast 2026 chosen title is "They Calle
 d Us the Enemy" by George Takei.  We will kick off this program by explor
 ing the traditional Japanese method of fish printing called Gyotaku (don't
  worry\, we're not using real fish!).  We will have copies of the book av
 ailable to hand out at the art event.  Later\, we will discuss the book a
 nd attend a live-stream author talk with George Takei.\nThursday April 16:
   Gyotaku Fish Printing and book handout\nTeen group 3:15pm-4:30pm\nAdult
  group 6:30pm-8:00pm\nThursday May 28:  Book Discussion\nTeen group 3:15p
 m-4:30pm\nAdult group 6:30pm-8:00pm\nSunday May 31:  Live-Stream Author T
 alk with George Takei\n2:00pm-4:00pm
LOCATION:Banks Public Library\, Jane Moore Community Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698655718b29ea2800ce6916
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
