BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Makerspace Open Lab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T193000
UID:69eea87afca21471b7f06734@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Makerspace Open Labs are for anyone who wants to check out the
  space and use our equipment to make cool things. Room assistants are avai
 lable to guide you in the basic use of the tools and technology. Come in w
 ith an idea and leave with a finished project! For more information about 
 the Makerspace and its resources\,\nsee here\n.\nMakerspace Open Labs take
  place on the following weekly schedule:\nTuesdays\n\, 5:30 - 7:30PM\nThur
 sdays\n\, 4:00 - 6:00PM\nSaturdays\n\, 10:00 AM - 1:00PM\nSundays\n\, 1:30
  - 5:30P\nEach month we provide the materials\, tools and instructions for
  a featured Makerspace project that everyone is invited to try.\nJune\n's 
 featured project is Clay Pot Mushrooms.\nIMPORTANT:\nAdults using the Make
 rspace for the first time need to\nsign a waiver\n\; people under the age 
 of 18 must have a waiver signed by a parent or guardian.\nYou can sign and
  submit waivers online here.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Makerspace
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69eea87afca21471b7f06734
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet the Artist| Conoce al Artista: Lynn M. Taylor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T193000
UID:69c6e00181b67dfe32af6b70@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us to meet Lynne M. Taylor\, a talented watercolor artist
  with nearly four decades of experience. Her art exhibition showcases her 
 stunning works that blend abstract and surrealistic symbolism\, focusing o
 n themes of nature\, spirituality\, and science. The exhibition features p
 ieces that have been highlighted on ISEPP program covers\, along with her 
 innovative Ice Painting series. Don’t miss the chance to view her award-
 winning artworks and learn about her journey as the owner of Laurelwood Ar
 t.\nThe exhibition runs from May 8 through June 30. Sponsored by the Corne
 lius Library Foundation.\nAcompáñanos a conocer a Lynne M. Taylor\, una 
 talentosa acuarelista con casi cuatro décadas de experiencia. Su exposici
 ón de arte muestra sus impresionantes obras que combinan simbolismo abstr
 acto y surrealista\, centrándose en temas como la naturaleza\, la espirit
 ualidad y la ciencia. La exposición presenta piezas que han sido destacad
 as en portadas de programas de ISEPP\, junto con su innovadora serie de Pi
 ntura sobre Hielo. No pierdas la oportunidad de ver sus obras galardonadas
  y conocer su trayectoria como propietaria de Laurelwood Art.\nLa exposici
 ón estará abierta del 8 de mayo al 30 de junio. Patrocinada por la Funda
 ción de la Biblioteca Cornelius.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c6e00181b67dfe32af6b70
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
