BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Baby Storytime
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T100000
UID:69d16e5eb6c4ac1fedca391a@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome infants 0-12 months and their caregivers!\nAttending B
 aby Storytime is a great way to build the bond between child and adult.\nI
 n this program you and your baby will sing songs\, play action rhymes\, an
 d grow together with books.\n15 minutes of playtime for babies and convers
 ation time for adults follows.\nThis is the spring session of this program
  and it runs March 31 –May 19\, 2026.\nWe understand how difficult it is
  to be punctual with a baby. Arrive anytime between 9:30a.m. – 10:00a.m
 . to enjoy this program. Playtime is just as beneficial as the storytime.
 \nLibrary opens at 10:00 a.m.\nBaby Storytime takes a break May 26 - Septe
 mber 1\, 2026. Fall session of Baby Storytime begins September 8\, 2026.
LOCATION:Sherwood Public Library\, Community Room\, main level.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d16e5eb6c4ac1fedca391a
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner ESL Class Provided by Goodwill Industries
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260601T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260601T190000
UID:69f23c10b6c4ac1fedcf9ea5@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This class is an introduction to basic grammar\, reading\, wri
 ting\, listening\, and speaking skills for students who can read and write
  in their first language. Students will receive a free textbook as a part
  of the class. We will work together to learn new vocabulary\, sentence pa
 tterns\, and communication using simple English.\nEsta clase es una introd
 ucción a las habilidades básicas de gramática\, lectura\, escritura\, c
 omprensión auditiva y expresión oral para estudiantes que pueden leer y 
 escribir en su primer idioma. Los estudiantes recibirán un libro de texto
  gratuito como parte de la clase. Trabajaremos juntos para aprender vocabu
 lario nuevo\, patrones de oraciones y comunicación usando un inglés simp
 le.
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Shute Park
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f23c10b6c4ac1fedcf9ea5
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
