BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What If Heroes Were Not Welcome Home? Exhibit from the Oregon Hist
 orical Society
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T235959
UID:69cc52928089f23c6765e3da@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This poignant exhibit examines the prejudice that Japanese Ame
 rican veterans from Hood River\, Oregon experienced upon their return home
  from serving our country in World War II. These American citizens served 
 heroically with the United States Armed Forces in the South Pacific and in
  Europe\, yet many of their families were unjustly incarcerated in concent
 ration camps on American soil.\nSee this exhibit at either the Cedar Mill 
 or Bethany Library. On display all month as part of\nOne Book\, One Coast\
 n.
LOCATION:Bethany Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cc52928089f23c6765e3da
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What If Heroes Were Not Welcome Home? Exhibit from the Oregon Hist
