BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:This is Vietnamese Portland Archive Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T190000
UID:699f427fec71a31f5b413283@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:We welcome you to join us for a Community Archive Day\, a comm
 unity collecting event including a presentation on preserving family histo
 ry and an invitation to bring any materials that you want help preserving.
  This is an opportunity to learn about archival best practices so that com
 munity members can better preserve their history. All are welcome.\nIn add
 ition to learning about archiving\, we invite you to help preserve and cel
 ebrate the rich history of the Vietnamese community in Portland. Do you ha
 ve material from a Vietnamese organization\, business or family in Portlan
 d—ledgers\, letters\, minutes\, photographs\, etc.? If so\, Vietnamese P
 ortland's team invites you to bring them to the library on Archive Day for
  review.
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f427fec71a31f5b413283
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Teen Botanical Watercolor Postcards
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T160000
UID:69d80d23b6c4ac1fedcb4b94@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join artist Elisa Mack to paint botanical postcards inspired b
 y your favorite plants or flowers! This workshop will focus on the basic t
 echniques essential for watercolor painting\, including composition\, brus
 h technique\, color mixing\, and more. No experience necessary\, all level
 s of artists are welcome to join! For tweens and teens entering grades 6-1
 2 in the fall. Registration required.
LOCATION:Aloha Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d80d23b6c4ac1fedcb4b94
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
