BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Storytime
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T120000
UID:69af4f5db0595799c0a1fe5c@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Storytime Wednesdays at 11:00 a.m.\nTime for stories\, bubbles
 \, and songs! Following storytime Mrs. Emily will teach children to identi
 fy and sound out letters of the alphabet and counting basics. Parents and 
 caregivers learn meaningful techniques that will help expand learning expe
 riences at home with your child. Drop in\, no registration required.\nIf a
 ccommodations would help you attend one of our library events or classes\,
  please ask. Our library events are always free!
LOCATION:North Plains Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af4f5db0595799c0a1fe5c
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Genealogical Society of Washington County
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T120000
UID:689d3c8f6ecff3faef536136@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Topic To Be Determined\nThe Ge\nnealogical Society is dedicate
 d to promoting the study of genealogy and the preservation of family herit
 age. Monthly meetings host speakers for instruction in family research. To
 pics range widely from local to international record search and use.\nChe
 ck out the website for more details:\nGenealogical Society of Wash. Co. we
 b site\nAttend in person or online.\nJoin Zoom Meeting:\nhttps://zoom.us/i
 /93563825582\nMeeting ID: 935 6382 5582
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/689d3c8f6ecff3faef536136
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drop-in Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260630T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260630T120000
UID:688a54b9639e1e9694a3d69a@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're a beginner trying to navigate your first smartp
 hone or a more experienced user looking to troubleshoot an issue with your
  computer or assemble a custom PC build\, we’re here to help. Drop-in to
  ask questions and receive one-on-one assistance with a variety of topics\
 , including but not limited to:\nBasic computer skills (e.g. how to use a 
 mouse\, open and close programs\, create and save documents)\nSetting up a
 nd using an email account\nUsing search engines and the internet\nTransfer
 ring files and photos between devices\nBasic smartphone and tablet skills 
 (e.g. how to make a call\, send a text message\, install and use an app)\n
 No matter your level of experience\, we welcome you to join us! No registr
 ation required. Please bring your device with you if you have one\, as thi
 s will allow us to better assist you with any specific issues you may be e
 xperiencing.
LOCATION:Aloha Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/688a54b9639e1e9694a3d69a
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
