BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Book Discussion: The Women by Kristin Hannah
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T190000
UID:697bbfacb0595799c0996d3c@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Read. Be inspired. Discuss.\nWe're hosting a book discussion i
 n person at the library. If you love to talk about the books you've read\
 , join us for a lively discussion of\nThe Women by Kristin Hannah\n\, wh
 ich may be available as an e-book and audiobook in Libby as well as physic
 al library copies which can be checked out. The first 10 people to regist
 er for this program can be given copies of the book provided generously by
  Friends of Sherwood Public Library.\nRegistration online is encouraged bu
 t not required.\nFrom the publisher:\nWomen can be heroes. When twenty-yea
 r-old nursing student Frances "Frankie" McGrath hears these unexpected wor
 ds\, it is a revelation. Raised on idyllic Coronado Island and sheltered b
 y her conservative parents\, she has always prided herself on doing the ri
 ght thing\, being a good girl. But in 1965 the world is changing\, and she
  suddenly imagines a different choice for her life. When her brother ships
  out to serve in Vietnam\, she impulsively joins the Army Nurse Corps and 
 follows his path. As green and inexperienced as the men sent to Vietnam to
  fight\, Frankie is overwhelmed by the chaos and destruction of war\, as w
 ell as the unexpected trauma of coming home to a changed and politically d
 ivided America.
LOCATION:Sherwood Public Library\, Community Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697bbfacb0595799c0996d3c
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Book Discussion: First Lie Wins by Ashley Elston
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T190000
UID:697bbefc4a9fd98b7f7aa765@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Read. Be inspired. Discuss.\nWe're hosting a book discussion i
 n person at the library. If you love to talk about the books you've read\
 , join us for a lively discussion of\nFirst Lie Wins by Ashley Elston\n\,
  which may be available as an e-book and audiobook in Libby as well as ph
 ysical library copies which can be checked out. The first 10 people to re
 gister for this program can be given copies of the book provided generousl
 y by Friends of Sherwood Public Library.\nRegistration online is encourage
 d but not required.\nFrom the publisher:\nEvie Porter has everything a nic
 e\, Southern girl could want: a perfect\, doting boyfriend\, a house with 
 a white picket fence and a garden\, a fancy group of friends. The only cat
 ch: Evie Porter doesn't exist. The identity comes first: Evie Porter. Once
  she's given a name and location by her mysterious boss Mr. Smith\, she le
 arns everything there is to know about the town and the people in it. Then
  the mark: Ryan Sumner. The last piece of the puzzle is the job. Evie isn'
 t privy to Mr. Smith's real identity\, but she knows this job will be diff
 erent. Ryan has gotten under her skin\, and she's starting to envision a d
 ifferent sort of life for herself. But Evie can't make any mistakes--espec
 ially after what happened last time. Because the one thing she's worked he
 r entire life to keep clean\, the one identity she could always go back to
 --her real identity--just walked right into this town. Evie Porter must st
 ay one step ahead of her past while making sure there's still a future in 
 front of her. The stakes couldn't be higher--but then\, Evie has always li
 ked a challenge...
LOCATION:Sherwood Public Library\, Community Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697bbefc4a9fd98b7f7aa765
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Navigator One-On-One Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260505T110000
UID:69b45f242866a5b48841dcb0@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Digital Navigator One-On-One Tech Help each Tuesday from 10:0
 0 a.m. -12:00 p.m. in the library.\nNeed help with digital questions or jo
 b searches? This free program is in partnership with American Connection C
 orps & The Washington County Broadband Action Team. Bring your own device 
 or use library computers.\nSign up for a 1 hour appointment.\nIf no appoin
 tments are scheduled drop in tech help will be available.\nThe Digital Nav
 igator Program (DNP) is a free service made possible by a partnership\nbet
 ween Washington County Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) and the Washin
 gton\nCounty Broadband Action Team. The DNP is funded in part by American 
 Connections\nCorps\, an AmeriCorps program dedicated to advancing economic
  prosperity by bridging\nthe digital divide. This project is being support
 ed\, in part\, by federal award number\nSLFRP0228 awarded to Washington Co
 unty by the U.S. Department of the Treasury.
LOCATION:North Plains Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b45f242866a5b48841dcb0
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
