BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Read to the Dogs/Lee a los perros
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T163000
UID:6932400b94297d36009e5b18@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to build your skills and confidence? Read aloud to a trai
 ned therapy dog (accompanied by their handler) in a private 20-minute sess
 ion. Grades K – 12.\n¿Quieres mejorar tus habilidades y tu confianza? I
 nscríbete para leer en voz alta a perros de terapia (acompañados por un 
 entrenador) en una sesión privada de 20 minutos. K – 12o grado.\nYou ma
 y sign up for one(1) Read to the Dogs session within a one(1) month period
 .
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6932400b94297d36009e5b18
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plant a Seed | Planta una Semilla
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T170000
UID:69e2e736defec6489cbe935c@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This year's Summer Reading Challenge theme is\, "Plant a Seed"
  and that's exactly what we're going to do for our first summer program! L
 earn all about germination and how tiny seeds become extraordinary plants 
 with some hands-on learning. Plant sunflower seeds\, build greenhouses\, a
 nd examine plants up close with microscopes from their flowers to their ro
 ots. Fun for all ages!\nEl tema del Reto de Lectura de Verano de este año
  es "Planta una semilla"\, ¡y eso es precisamente lo que haremos en nuest
 ro primer programa de verano! Aprende todo sobre la germinación y cómo l
 as diminutas semillas se convierten en plantas extraordinarias con activid
 ades prácticas. Planta semillas de girasol\, construye invernaderos y exa
 mina las plantas de cerca con microscopios\, desde sus flores hasta sus ra
 íces. ¡Diversión para todas las edades!
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e2e736defec6489cbe935c
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:One Book\, One Coast Watch Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T150000
UID:69e69f27defec6489cbf2180@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Aloha Community Library is joining more than 130 library s
 ystems \non the West Coast for a shared community reading experience! Libr
 ary \nusers at all participating locations are invited to read the graphic
  \nmemoir\nThey Called Us Enemy\n\, recounting actor\, author\, and \nacti
 vist George Takei’s childhood imprisonment within American \nincarcerati
 on camps during World War II.\nRequest your copy on hold from our catalog\
 n\, or\naccess the e-book version on Libby\nimmediately – unlimited digi
 tal copies will be available through Saturday 6/6!\nFinished reading and r
 eady to discuss?\nFind discussion opportunities\nat various WCCLS librarie
 s!\nOne Book\, One Coast will close with a special author talk hosted on \
 nSunday 5/31 at the East Los Angeles Library and featuring George Takei. \
 nGeorge will discuss the experiences that led to the creation of his \nmem
 oir\, what it means to be a good neighbor and citizen in the face of \nove
 rwhelming challenges\, and how shared books and stories build stronger\n c
 ommunities.\nRegister to watch the livestream online\n\, or join us here a
 t the Aloha Community Library for a watch party! Our doors will open at 1:
 45pm.
LOCATION:Aloha Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e69f27defec6489cbf2180
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
