BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Technology Open Lab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T150000
UID:698fa0b93cc3e0c9ecb92e10@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Need help getting started with e-books\, adding an app to your
  smartphone\, or updating your email contacts? Volunteers will be availabl
 e at Open Lab to answer questions. Bring your own computer\, tablet\, cell
 phone\, or e-reader with you to get assistance or use one of our laptops t
 o practice. Be sure to have any usernames and passwords available for acc
 ounts you need help navigating.\nOur spring session of Technology Open Lab
  meets 1-3 pm on Thursdays\, 3/12\, 3/26\, 4/9\, 4/23\, 5/14\, and 5/28.\n
 Drop-in sessions\, no registration is required\, but there is limited spac
 e each session.\nFor more information please call 503-644-0043 or ask staf
 f at any service desk.
LOCATION:Cedar Mill Library\, Main Library Floor
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698fa0b93cc3e0c9ecb92e10
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:4-H Explorstation Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260506T163000
UID:69616b6bc967cb412080fe16@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Kristen Moore\, Assistant Professor of Practice\, 4-H Yo
 uth Development\, Oregon State Extension Service\, Washington County\, fo
 r an hour of STEAM (science\, technology\, engineering\, arts\, math).\nF
 or more than 100 years\, 4-H has assisted youth in acquiring knowledge\, d
 eveloping life skills\, and forming attitudes that will enable them to fin
 d their "spark" and become self-directing\, productive members of society.
  4-H is an informal\, practical\, learn-by-doing educational program for y
 outh.
LOCATION:North Plains Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69616b6bc967cb412080fe16
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Read to the Dogs/Lee a los perros
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T163000
UID:6932400b94297d36009e5b11@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to build your skills and confidence? Read aloud to a trai
 ned therapy dog (accompanied by their handler) in a private 20-minute sess
 ion. Grades K – 12.\n¿Quieres mejorar tus habilidades y tu confianza? I
 nscríbete para leer en voz alta a perros de terapia (acompañados por un 
 entrenador) en una sesión privada de 20 minutos. K – 12o grado.\nYou ma
 y sign up for one(1) Read to the Dogs session within a one(1) month period
 .
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6932400b94297d36009e5b11
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
