BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Storytime
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260610T120000
UID:69af4f5db0595799c0a1fe5f@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Storytime Wednesdays at 11:00 a.m.\nTime for stories\, bubbles
 \, and songs! Following storytime Mrs. Emily will teach children to identi
 fy and sound out letters of the alphabet and counting basics. Parents and 
 caregivers learn meaningful techniques that will help expand learning expe
 riences at home with your child. Drop in\, no registration required.\nIf a
 ccommodations would help you attend one of our library events or classes\,
  please ask. Our library events are always free!
LOCATION:North Plains Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af4f5db0595799c0a1fe5f
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Inclusive Storytime
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T101500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T110000
UID:691d0231a64b7d0d61f7dd93@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Limited to 15 children\, ages 3-5\, and their parents and care
 givers. Kids with varying learning styles and abilities come together in a
  safe and supportive environment. Children who may need visual/communicati
 on supports\, a more predictable routine\, or adapted materials due to a m
 otor impairment are welcome. Pre-register at\nmpebly@pdx.edu\n\; we can se
 nd materials home ahead of time.\nBilingual sessions are held at Shute Par
 k Library on 1st and 3rd Fridays.
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/691d0231a64b7d0d61f7dd93
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full STEAM Ahead: Tessellation Stamps
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T173000
UID:69e2c267bd5c392c7644e8f1@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Full STEAM Ahead is a series of classes where we will explore 
 science concepts through art projects.\nMay brings in so many repeating pa
 tterns in nature like flowers\, leaves and butterflies. This month we will
  see how to make stamps that make patterns when stamped across the page.\n
 For students in grades 3-5. Registration is required. Held in the Makerspa
 ce.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e2c267bd5c392c7644e8f1
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
