UID:69c86eee1e64afd01e655f30@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Valerie Gillis goes missing in Maine while hiking the Appalach
 ian Trail.  The mystery at the center of this addictive novel is complemen
 ted by vibrant descriptions of Valerie’s environment\, endearing portray
 als of the characters involved in her search\, and moving explorations of 
 complex mother-daughter relationships.\nReserve it\nhere\n:  Also availa
 ble in large print\, eBook\, downloadable audiobook\, and audiobook CD\nJo
 in online by clicking here:\nhttps://bit.ly/ACLbkclub\nOr call 253-215-878
 2 to join by phone.\nMeeting ID: 924 6989 8432 & Passcode: 037016\nIf you 
 would like to read ahead\, here is the book club’s schedule for the rest
  of 2026:\nMay 6th (online) & 7th (in person) -\nHeartwood\nby Amity Gaige
 \nJune 3rd (online) & 4th (in person) -\nThe Anthropocene Reviewed\nby Joh
 n Green\nJuly & August - Break\nSeptember 9th (online) & 10th (in person) 
 -\nTress of the Emerald Sea\nby Brandon Sanderson\nOctober 7th (online) & 
 8th (in person) -\nRemarkably Bright Creatures\nby Shelby Van Pelt\nNovemb
 er 4th (online) & 5th (in person) -\nBad Cree\nby Jessica Johns\nDecember 
 - Break
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c86eee1e64afd01e655f30
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
