BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Navigator Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T153000
UID:69c85287e2a2952aed0b4b15@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you need one-on-one assistance with your digital questions?
  A trusted guide can help you learn about home connectivity\, devices\, an
 d digital skills. Register for a slot. Bring your device or use a library 
 computer.\nRegistrants will be contacted for more details.\nSlots are 30-4
 0 minutes long. Sign up for your preferred time slot: 3\, 3:45\, 4:30\, or
  5:15. [We do not have a waitlist\; please call or visit the library the 
 day off the Digital Navigator appointment to check availability.]\nThe Dig
 ital Navigator Program (DNP) is a free service made possible by a partners
 hip between Washington County Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) and the
  American Connections Corps\, who empowers its members and the communities
  they serve to address digital disparities and create lasting change.
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library\, Enter via the rec center's main e
 ntrance and walk through the building to the library. Or use the doorbell 
 at the door by the library.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c85287e2a2952aed0b4b15
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seed Paper | Papel con Semillas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T190000
UID:69e2e72bc1cf6f9a75862383@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Recycled paper is certainly better for the environment than yo
 ur regular tree paper\, but that doesn't mean we can't get creative and ha
 ve some fun with it too. Learn how to make your own recycled paper infused
  with usable seeds! Once the paper has fulfilled its use\, you can plant i
 t in the ground where the paper helps the seeds sprout and the entire she
 et decomposes back into the earth bringing forth new life!\nThis program i
 s for teens aged 13-18.\nEl papel reciclado es sin duda mejor para el medi
 o ambiente que el papel convencional\, pero eso no significa que no podamo
 s ser creativos y divertirnos con él. ¡Aprende a hacer tu propio papel r
 eciclado con semillas! Una vez que el papel haya cumplido su función\, pu
 edes plantarlo en la tierra\; el papel ayudará a que las semillas germine
 n y la hoja se descompondrá\, reintegrándose a la tierra y dando vida a 
 nueva vida.\nEste programa está dirigido a adolescentes de 13 a 18 años.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e2e72bc1cf6f9a75862383
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
