DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T174500
UID:69c85287e2a2952aed0b4b18@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you need one-on-one assistance with your digital questions?
  A trusted guide can help you learn about home connectivity\, devices\, an
 d digital skills. Register for a slot. Bring your device or use a library 
 computer.\nRegistrants will be contacted for more details.\nSlots are 30-4
 0 minutes long. Sign up for your preferred time slot: 3\, 3:45\, 4:30\, or
  5:15. [We do not have a waitlist\; please call or visit the library the 
 day off the Digital Navigator appointment to check availability.]\nThe Dig
 ital Navigator Program (DNP) is a free service made possible by a partners
 hip between Washington County Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) and the
  American Connections Corps\, who empowers its members and the communities
  they serve to address digital disparities and create lasting change.
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library\, Enter via the rec center's main e
 ntrance and walk through the building to the library. Or use the doorbell 
 at the door by the library.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c85287e2a2952aed0b4b18
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bloodwork NW Blood Drive
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T160000
UID:697a603c4a9fd98b7f7a6299@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Every summer\, hospitals having blood supplies on hand is crit
 ical during the\n100 deadliest days\nbetween Memorial Day and Labor Day. D
 uring this time\, more folks are taking vacations and not donating blood a
 s frequently\, and simultaneously hospitals tend to see an uptick in traum
 as and emergencies with more people adventuring and road tripping where mo
 re accidents happen.\nThe library is hosting another Bloodworks NW mobile 
 drive on Friday\, May 8\, from 10:00 am to 4:00 pm. Sign up for your 1-hou
 r appointment online at\nhttps://donate.bloodworksnw.or...\nPlus\, donors 
 at this drive who are 18+ and complete a post-donation only entry form at\
 nwww.bloodworksnw.org/win\nhave a chance to win a getaway to Hawaii!\nMust
  be 16+ to donate. Be sure to eat a hearty meal and drink plenty of fluids
  prior to donating.
LOCATION:Forest Grove City Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697a603c4a9fd98b7f7a6299
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
