BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:One Book One Coast Book Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260504T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260504T153000
UID:69b590e277edebcd1f44e46b@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the largest book club on the West Coast!\nWest Slo
 pe Community Library will be hosting a discussion of\nThey Called Us Enemy
 \nby George Takei.\nOne Book\, One Coast\nis a collaborative program uniti
 ng a \nwide network of West Coast libraries in a shared celebration of \nl
 iteracy\, learning\, community\, and civil discourse. From April 1 through
 \n May 31st\, all participating libraries will read and discuss\nThey Call
 ed Us Enemy\nby George Takei.\nThey Called Us Enemy\nis a graphic memoir \
 nrecounting actor/author/activist George Takei’s childhood imprisoned \n
 within American concentration camps during World War II. Confronting \nque
 stions of patriotism\, family\, loyalty\, and community\, George’s work 
 \nis a stunning examination of what it means to be American\, both then an
 d\n now.\nRead\nThey Called Us Enemy\nat WCCLS
LOCATION:West Slope Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b590e277edebcd1f44e46b
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
