BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Page Turners Book Club: The Anthropocene Reviewed
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T193000
UID:69f69c432866a5b4884c5333@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this collection of bite-sized and snackable essays\, John G
 reen (bestselling author of\nEverything is Tuberculosis)\nexplores and rat
 es marvels of our world\, like Halley’s Comet and Dr. Pepper. Each piece
  showcases his endearing mix of humor and wisdom\, and illuminates larger 
 truths about seeing the world with curiosity and compassion.\nReserve it\n
 here\n:  Also available in eBook\, downloadable audiobook\, and audioboo
 k CD\nIf you would like to read ahead\, here is the book club’s schedule
  for the rest of 2026:\nJune 3rd (online) & 4th (in-person) - The Anthropo
 cene Reviewed\nhttps://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S143C3867359\nby 
 John Green\nJuly - Break\nAugust - Break\nSeptember 9th (online) & 10th (i
 n-person) - Tress of the Emerald Sea\nhttps://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/r
 ecord/S143C4189016\nby Brandon Sanderson\nOctober 7th (online) & 8th (in-p
 erson) - Remarkably Bright Creatures\nhttps://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/r
 ecord/S143C4054983\nby Shelby Van Pelt\nNovember 4th (online) & 5th (in-pe
 rson) - Bad Cree\nhttps://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S143C4157107\n
 by Jessica Johns\nDecember - Break
LOCATION:Aloha Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f69c432866a5b4884c5333
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
