BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cosplay Meet-up
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T113000
UID:69966ed54a9fd98b7f7efad7@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Collaboratory to learn about crafting costumes
  for cosplaying! All skill levels and skill sets are welcome.  We have bas
 ic supplies and equipment.  Drop-in anytime and bring your own projects.\n
 Ages 12+.\nThe space is dedicated to this particular activity\, no regist
 ration required.\n#Collaboratory
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69966ed54a9fd98b7f7efad7
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Garden Gnomes du Plume: Making Magic: Crafting a Magic System for 
 Your World
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T193000
UID:69d9762d5c04bc0fc06203a5@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This month our writer's group meeting will be all about "Makin
 g Magic: Crafting a Magic System for Your World". Led by our very own memb
 er\, Ian J. Frank!\nA captivating magic system can significantly enhance 
 any work of fantasy\, drawing the reader deeper into the world that we\, a
 s authors\, have crafted for them. How do you effectively incorporate thes
 e elements into your own work? Are you just beginning to explore these rea
 lms? Or perhaps\, like myself\, have you embarked on your writing adventur
 e without fully comprehending the intricacies of magic systems\, only to d
 iscover their significance later on? In this session\, we will delve into 
 the characteristics of magic systems and explore some of the guidelines th
 at have proven instrumental in refining my own magic system.\nBio:\nIan J.
  Frank\nis an author\, world-builder\, artist\, engineer\, community advoc
 ate\, and general nerd. He is currently learning the answer to the questio
 n he posed in 2022: just how long could it really take to write his first 
 novel? He is an avid consumer of stories in all forms — loving the fanta
 sy\, sci-fi\, and mystery/thriller genres. He lives in Portland\, Oregon\,
  with his wife and their two furry children.
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library\, Our writer's group meets in the l
 ibrary's event space\, GeRoom #7 (next to the locker rooms). Enter via the
  main entrance and walk through the rec center.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d9762d5c04bc0fc06203a5
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Makerspace Open Lab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260609T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260609T193000
UID:69eea87afca21471b7f06738@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Makerspace Open Labs are for anyone who wants to check out the
  space and use our equipment to make cool things. Room assistants are avai
 lable to guide you in the basic use of the tools and technology. Come in w
 ith an idea and leave with a finished project! For more information about 
 the Makerspace and its resources\,\nsee here\n.\nMakerspace Open Labs take
  place on the following weekly schedule:\nTuesdays\n\, 5:30 - 7:30PM\nThur
 sdays\n\, 4:00 - 6:00PM\nSaturdays\n\, 10:00 AM - 1:00PM\nSundays\n\, 1:30
  - 5:30P\nEach month we provide the materials\, tools and instructions for
  a featured Makerspace project that everyone is invited to try.\nJune\n's 
 featured project is Clay Pot Mushrooms.\nIMPORTANT:\nAdults using the Make
 rspace for the first time need to\nsign a waiver\n\; people under the age 
 of 18 must have a waiver signed by a parent or guardian.\nYou can sign and
  submit waivers online here.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Makerspace
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69eea87afca21471b7f06738
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
