BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Simple Estate Planning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T130000
UID:69c4686e8089f23c6764a9e5@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Registration encouraged\nCheryl Gill\, author of\nA Very Simpl
 e Estate Planning Guide\,\nwill explain how to make the process of estate 
 planning as simple and stress-free as possible.\nThe following are some of
  the topics that will be covered:\nWhat is estate planning and how do you 
 get started\nWhat are the three things everyone needs to have\nWhat are th
 e easiest ways to keep assets out of probate\nWhat are the most common mis
 takes people make\nAbout the presenter: Gill ventured into estate planning
  for personal reasons\, but quickly found the information available to be 
 confusing and overwhelming. Hearing the same frustration voiced by many ot
 hers motivated her to create a guide to help people overcome the stumbling
  blocks that keep them from moving forward. With 25 plus years in the real
  estate and legal worlds\, her aim was simple: create a book that presents
  this topic in a way that everyone can understand and walks them through t
 he process to reach their goal.\nCopies of Gill’s book will also be avai
 lable to purchase.\nCopies are also available in the WCCLS catalog.
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library\, This event will be held in the Ga
 rden Home Library's event room (GeRoom #7)\, which is by the rec center lo
 cker rooms.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c4686e8089f23c6764a9e5
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Repair Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T160000
UID:69bdbf5f1e64afd01e63a3f0@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Saturday\, June 20th\, for a free community repair 
 event. Volunteers will be available in the Rogers Room from 1:00 - 4:00 PM
  to look at and possibly fix household items - small appliances\, electron
 ics\, computers and mobile devices\, toys\, bikes\, clothing\, home décor
 \, small furniture\, lamps\, vacuums\, jewelry\, etc. Please no gas-powere
 d equipment\, TVs\, or microwaves.\nLimit two items per attendee\n.\nWant 
 to sign up your item for repair? Interested in volunteering at the Repair 
 Fair? Follow this\nlink\n!
LOCATION:Forest Grove City Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bdbf5f1e64afd01e63a3f0
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marbling Art | Arte del Marmoleado
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T170000
UID:69bdbf805a2d780f42c4444f@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You probably already know about all of the fun and unique way
 s you can paint your nails\, but did you know nail polish is also really 
 good for marbling art as well? We'll show you how to use nail polish to cr
 eate colorful\, mesmerizing patterns that mix and flow with each other\, 
 then apply that paint to paper and even accessories! This program is for 
 adults.\nSeguramente ya conoces todas las formas divertidas y originales d
 e pintarte las uñas\, pero ¿sabías que el esmalte de uñas también es 
 ideal para la técnica del marmoleado? Te mostraremos cómo usar el esmalt
 e para crear patrones coloridos y fascinantes que se mezclan y fluyen entr
 e sí\, ¡y luego aplicar esa pintura sobre papel e incluso accesorios! E
 ste programa es para adultos.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bdbf805a2d780f42c4444f
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
