BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bricks for Better Brains Monthly Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T160000
UID:69c85305b6c4ac1fedc8cf73@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bricks for Better Brains© encourages older people to explore 
 creativity\, strengthen social connections\, and take advantage of tactile
  stimulation.\nParticipants will work on a set or free build. All material
 s will be provided.\nAbout our presenter and the founder of Bricks for Bet
 ter Brains: Natalia Kasperovich is a university-educated chemical engineer
 \, community volunteer\, educator\, and most importantly\, a lifelong lear
 ner. She has an Associate Degree in Gerontology from Portland Community C
 ollege. She is a passionate advocate for continuous and self-motivated lea
 rning\, intergenerational understanding\, diversity\, and inclusivity.\nRe
 gistration is encouraged\; but not required. {It helps us know how many su
 pplies and how many tables and chairs to have set up beforehand.}
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library\, This event takes place in the lib
 rary's event room\, which is located next to the rec center's locker rooms
 .
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c85305b6c4ac1fedc8cf73
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:One Book\, One Coast: They Called Us Enemy Book Group Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T120000
UID:69c4329b81b67dfe32aeee5c@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us to discuss the graphic memoir\nThey Called Us Enemy by
  George Takei\n.\n As part of One Book\, One Coast\, we will be reading th
 is account of \nGeorge Takei's childhood as his family was imprisoned in a
 n American \nconcentration camp during World War II.\nRegistration recomme
 nded to get a reminder email.\nThis is part of our One Book\, One Coast re
 ading program with events all month long. For all events\, visit our\nwebs
 ite\n.
LOCATION:Cedar Mill Library\, Elm and Oak Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c4329b81b67dfe32aeee5c
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Caregiver Resource Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T150000
UID:69cc59a98089f23c6765e55b@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of Older Americans Month\, Washington County Di
 sability\, Aging & Veteran Services invites family and friend caregivers t
 o connect with over 20 local resources\, support services\, and community 
 partners dedicated to helping you care for your aging loved ones. Explore 
 educational materials\, meet experts\, and discover programs designed to s
 upport you in caregiving. Community presentations will be held at 1:30\, 2
 :15\, and 3 PM in the auditorium. These 30-minute sessions will provide pr
 actical guidance on navigating community support. Find more details about 
 presentation topics and the full schedule at www.washingtoncountyor.gov/da
 vs/activities-workshops-and-conferences. This event is designed for unpaid
  family and friends supporting an aging individual in our community\, not 
 professional caregivers.
LOCATION:Beaverton City Library\, Meeting Rooms A & B
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cc59a98089f23c6765e55b
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tales to Tails
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T154500
UID:69d19f8ef29b90618efd6c48@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Read to a certified therapy dog in a stress-free environment\,
  now at West Slope Community Library!\nSign-up for a 20-minute reading ses
 sion.\nThis program will help improve your child's reading skills and they
  get to make a new friend by reading aloud to a therapy dog.\nThe dogs and
  handlers are from\nDove Lewis Portland Area Canine Therapy Teams\nand\nPe
 t Partners®
LOCATION:West Slope Community Library\, Check in at Front Desk
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d19f8ef29b90618efd6c48
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
