BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Take & Make Craft: Koinobori Wind Socks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260531T235959
UID:69ea51de66c3387a9d07af7a@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:“Koinobori\n\, or carp streamers\, are a beloved symbol of C
 hildren’s Day in Japan\, celebrated annually on May 5th. These colorful 
 windsocks in the shape of carp are traditionally flown outside homes\, sch
 ools\, and public spaces to wish children strength\, health\, and success.
  The koinobori are designed to flutter and swim in the wind\, resembling c
 arp swimming upstream\, a metaphor for perseverance and growth.”\nhttps:
 //travel.rakuten.com/contents/usa/en-us/guide/koinobori/\nKit includes:\nP
 recut koinobori windsock\n2 washable markers\nCardstock strip\nLength of s
 tring for hanging\nYou provide:\nGlue\nScissors or hole punch\nMore marker
 s\, watercolor paints\, or whatever arts & crafts supplies you choose to a
 dd!\nRegister\nto reserve your kit and pick it up at West Slope Library at
  your convenience any time from May1st-31st* during the library's open hou
 rs. Some kits will also be available for pick up at the library\, no reser
 vation required.\nThese kits are graciously sponsored by the Cultural Coal
 ition of Washington County and the Oregon Cultural Trust.\nPlease limit 1
  kit per person\n.\nWe can't wait to see what you create! Send your pictur
 e by email to\nwestslope@wccls.org\nor tag us on Instagram @gardenhomecomm
 unitylibrary\n*Reserved kits not picked up by May 31st will be offered to
  those on the waitlist or first come\, first serve at the library.
LOCATION:West Slope Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ea51de66c3387a9d07af7a
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
