BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall prevention\, balance\, and healthy living
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260630T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260630T120000
UID:69f3d45ef29b90618effff65@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Falls are the leading cause of injury and death among Oregonia
 ns age 65 and older.\nThe  goal of this free workshop - led by Kayt Zundel
  MPA\, MS from Legacy Health Systems - is to provide older adults informa
 tion and tools to help prevent a fall and to encourage living an active an
 d healthy life. Topics covered include concussions and brain health\, medi
 cation interactions\, common reasons for falling\, home safety\, exercise\
 , and easy steps you can take to prevent a fall.\nIt covers transportation
  and pedestrian related issues\, and we walk through a couple of the balan
 ce exercises.\nFree fall prevention items will be provided to participants
 .\nRegistration is required.
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library\, This event will be hosted in the 
 library's event room (GeRoom #7)\, next to the rec center locker rooms. En
 ter via the main entrance and walk through the rec center to the event.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f3d45ef29b90618effff65
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bricks for Better Brains Monthly Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T163000
UID:69f3d53224bd39b0b5e90ffd@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bricks for Better Brains© encourages older people to explore 
 creativity\, strengthen social connections\, and take advantage of tactile
  stimulation.\nParticipants will work on a set or free build. All material
 s will be provided.\nAbout our presenter and the founder of Bricks for Bet
 ter Brains: Natalia Kasperovich is a university-educated chemical engineer
 \, community volunteer\, educator\, and most importantly\, a lifelong lear
 ner. She has an Associate Degree in Gerontology from Portland Community C
 ollege. She is a passionate advocate for continuous and self-motivated lea
 rning\, intergenerational understanding\, diversity\, and inclusivity.\nRe
 gistration is encouraged\; but not required. {It helps us know how to set 
 up beforehand.}
LOCATION:Garden Home Community Library\, Enter via the rec center's main e
 ntrance and walk through the building to the library's event room (GeRoom 
 #7) by the locker rooms.
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f3d53224bd39b0b5e90ffd
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
